# Token efficiency

Three complementary layers. Setup: `pnpm agent-tools:setup`. Refresh graph: `pnpm graphify:update`.

| Layer | Tool | What it saves |
|-------|------|----------------|
| **Code read** | graphify | Grep/read tokens on exploration |
| **Shell output** | RTK | Verbose git/test/lint output (Cursor hook on Shell) |
| **Prose** | caveman | Filler in chat and summaries |

## Read path (exploration)

Use this cascade — do not skip to Read/Grep/Glob for orientation:

1. **`./.venv-graphify/bin/graphify query "<question>"`** — scoped subgraph (`path`, `explain` for traces)
2. **Layer search** — [pixelanea-agent-tools.mdc](./pixelanea-agent-tools.mdc) when you know the layer
3. **Targeted Read** — only files graphify/search already identified

After code edits: `pnpm graphify:update` (or `./scripts/graphify-update.sh`).

## Shell path

RTK rewrites Shell tool calls globally. Prefer shell for git, tests, lint, docker — not raw Read/Grep for the same data.

Explicit when needed: `rtk git status`, `rtk vitest`, `rtk cargo test`, `rtk pytest`.

## Prose path

- **Chat:** terse fragments per [caveman.mdc](./caveman.mdc) — no tool-call narration, no decorative tables
- **Step files** (`01_*.md`, …): structured segments (Goal / Outcome / Files) but concise — link paths, no code dumps
- **Persisted product text:** commits, code, Gherkin, API specs — normal prose (caveman off)

## Subagents

Every Task prompt that explores code or runs shell must include:

```text
Token efficiency: graphify query before grep/read; layer search when layer known; terse Outcome segments; shell for git/test/lint (RTK).
```

Orchestrators: pass the line above in every worker delegation.
